source      RDKit's ForceFields::CrystalFF::getExperimentalTorsions (patched build), read through
            bb-rdkit's cxx bridge. Not exposed to RDKit's Python API in the form the engine uses:
            GetExperimentalTorsions returns only SMARTS-matched library torsions, while the bridge
            reads CrystalFFDetails, which also carries basic-knowledge planarity terms and the
            improperAtoms list. The bridge calls the function and copies its results.
patch       force constants 80.0 and 130.9 are Divya's amide reweighting; see
            rdkit-patch/divya_amide_torsions.diff
